{:id "adr-2605312345-kotoba-datom-first-class-canonical-state" :title "ADR-2605312345: kotoba Datom as First-Class Canonical State — IPFS reframed as block backend, MST as ingress/interop wire, Base L2 as trust anchor" :status "proposed" :doc-type "adr" :topic "storage-substrate" :authoritative true :last-verified "2026-05-31" :priority 5.0 :axis "architecture" :weight 0.65 :priority-note "Doctrine-clarifying successor to ADR-2605262130. Elevates the kotoba Datom log (content-addressed, immutable EAVT Datalog — Datomic-isomorphic) to the FIRST-CLASS canonical state primitive, resolving the mismatch between kotoba's own self-definition ('the distributed Datom DB is the source of truth') and the root-repo doctrine that listed MST+IPFS+L2 as 'State' with the Datom as a regenerable projection. No constitutional invariant is changed — only the layering/authority direction is made explicit. IPFS/MST/Base L2 are retained but reframed as subordinate physical/interop layers under the Datom." :authoritative-for ["canonical state primitive = kotoba Datom log (content-addressed EAVT Datalog)" "reframing of IPFS as Datom block backend (cold tier / DHT)" "reframing of AT Protocol MST as ingress + interop wire format (not canonical state home)" "reframing of Base L2 as trust anchor over the Datom commit-DAG root"] :depends-on ["adr-2605262130-kotoba-storage-substrate-unification" "adr-2605172000-etzhayyim-kotoba-substrate" "adr-2605215000-etzhayyim-inference-murakumo-only-no-runpod" "adr-2605181100-mst-encrypted-records-signal-keywrap"] :related ["adr-2605231400-kotoba-datomic-holochain-iso-substrate" "adr-2605231500-kotoba-datomic-projection" "adr-2605231902-feed-post-membrane-and-feed-discover-projection" "adr-2605171800-langgraph-mst-ipfs-l2-anchor-pipeline" "adr-2605231525-no-server-key-religious-corp-architecture" "adr-2605192245-etzhayyim-global-land-sovereignty"] :supersedes [] :superseded-by [] :file "2605312345-kotoba-datom-first-class-canonical-state.md"}
{:id "adr-2605312330-giemon-part-graph-sbom-kotoba-fleet-cve-svelte" :title "ADR-2605312330: giemon part graph — EDN ledger → CycloneDX SBOM → kotoba EAVT → cross-robot fleet + purl-CVE vuln-match + Svelte surfaces" :status "accepted" :doc-type "adr" :topic "giemon-part-graph-sbom-kotoba" :authoritative true :last-verified "2026-05-31" :priority 4.5 :axis "architecture" :weight 0.4 :priority-note "Follow-on to ADR-2605312300 (giemon kabitori sim). Answers the founder's question — are robot CAD parts linked per-part to product/manufacturer via SBOM, and is it organized in edn/Datomic/kotoba? — by building the full pipeline: a Datomic-style EDN part ledger, a CycloneDX SBOM generator, ingest into the kotoba EAVT store (Datomic-class, no Kotoba/Datomic per ADR-2605262130), a cross-robot fleet graph (kabitori + Giemon Otete), the legacy-Kotoba/Datomic-SBOM→kotoba bridge, purl-keyed SBOM↔CVE vuln-match (the kotoba-native vertex_sbom_vuln_match), and browser surfaces in the isekai SvelteKit app. All claims verified by direct cargo-test / live kotoba serve." :authoritative-for ["giemon part-ledger EDN schema (parts.edn) + sbom_gen.py generator" "giemon SBOM → kotoba EAVT ingest contract (kg.ingest_batch, kg/claim/part/*)" "cross-robot fleet part graph (kabitori + giemon-otete) in kotoba" "legacy Kotoba/Datomic SBOM → kotoba bridge (cyclonedx_to_kotoba.py) + column mapping" "purl-keyed SBOM↔CVE vuln-match materialization (VulnMatch entities)" "giemon Svelte surfaces (/giemon, /giemon.htm, /fleet) in etzhayyim-project-isekai"] :depends-on ["adr-2605312300-giemon-kabitori-mold-removal-probe-sim" "adr-2605262130-kotoba-storage-substrate-unification"] :related ["adr-2605051430-drive-cad-jbeam-sbom-pipeline"] :supersedes [] :superseded-by [] :file "2605312330-giemon-part-graph-sbom-kotoba-fleet-cve-svelte.md"}
{:id "adr-2605312300-giemon-kabitori-mold-removal-probe-sim" :title "ADR-2605312300: giemon kabitori (黴取り) mold-removal probe — sim + wall-obstacle contact extension + mold-erosion field" :status "accepted" :doc-type "adr" :topic "giemon-kabitori-mold-removal-sim" :authoritative true :last-verified "2026-05-31" :priority 5.0 :axis "architecture" :weight 0.4 :priority-note "Founder asked to design + simulate a machine to remove EXISTING mold from A/C units, building gaps, and HVAC ducts, on the giemon / kami-engine (Omniverse/PhysX/Isaac-class clean-room) stack. Reframes the popular 'nanomachine' ask as an achievable steerable cleaning probe, builds it as a giemon variant on kami-genesis, and extends the engine with static wall/box obstacles (so a duct/gap can be boxed in) plus an application-layer mold-coverage erosion field (since the rigid solver has no erodible-material solver). All claims verified by direct cargo-test." :authoritative-for ["giemon kabitori mold-removal probe articulation (6-DOF mixed prismatic+revolute) + scene URDF" "kami-genesis static environment obstacles (Obstacle::Plane / Obstacle::Aabb) in the contact solver" "kabitori mold-coverage erosion model (MoldField) at the giemon application layer" "honest scope boundary: rigid-body + ground/wall contact only; no biofilm/fluid solver yet"] :depends-on ["adr-2605311800-kami-genesis-3d-spatial-articulation-and-contact-solver" "adr-2605311500-kami-genesis-physics-validation-and-isaac-clean-room-surface" "adr-2605261800-nvidia-omniverse-stack-api-compat" "adr-2605261600-robotics-simulation-substrate-r0"] :related [] :supersedes [] :superseded-by [] :file "2605312300-giemon-kabitori-mold-removal-probe-sim.md"}
